74
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:47,940
Oh, my God!

75
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:47,940
I have a feeling it's gonna be a girl.

76
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,770
Phoebe, you were sure Ben was gonna be a girl.

77
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,150
Have you seen him throw a ball'?

78
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:58,610
Is Rachel here?

79
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:58,610
Uh, I think she's still asleep.

80
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:01,030
Hey, hey, hey. How did it go with you guys last night?

81
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,370
She seemed pretty pissed at you.

82
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:06,620
We, uh... You know, we worked things out.

83
00:05:07,790 --> 00:05:10,630
What's that smile? Did something happen with you two?

84
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:13,300
Hey, I'm not one to kiss and tell.

85
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:17,300
Uh, but I'm also not one to have sex and shut up. We totally did it.

86
00:05:18,970 --> 00:05:20,390
Oh, my God. You and Rachel?

87
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:23,470
I know, it's pretty great.

88
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:23,470
So, what does that mean?

89
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:26,310
Are you guys getting back together?

90
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:26,310
Oh, I don't know.

91
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,810
We didn't really get to talk.

92
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,810
But do you want to get back together?

93
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:32,020
I don't know.

94
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:35,820
It was incredible. I mean, it just felt so right.

95
00:05:35,990 --> 00:05:41,120
When I was holding her, I mean, I never wanted to let her go.

96
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,200
Know what? Yeah, I do. I want to be together.

97
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:45,660
Yay!

98
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:45,660
Shh!

99
00:05:45,910 --> 00:05:47,410
Yay!

100
00:05:48,410 --> 00:05:50,710
So is she still going to Paris?

101
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:53,800
Wow, I hadn't thought of that. I hope not.

102
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:57,720
This is, like, the best day ever. Ever. You guys might get back together.

103
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:01,010
Monica and Chandler get their baby. There are chicks and ducks...

104
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:03,010
...in the world again.

105
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:06,310
Oh. I feel like I'm in a musical.

106
00:06:08,350 --> 00:06:11,810
When the sun comes up Bright and beamin'

107
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,020
And the moon comes

108
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:15,900
Morning.

109
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:15,900
Guess you'll never know how it ends.

110
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,860
Hey.

111
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,860
Hi.

112
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:22,110
Hi. How'd you sleep?

113
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:22,110
Good. You?

114
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:25,740
Good.

115
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:25,740
I'll bet you did.

116
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:29,500
Uh, would you guys mind giving us a minute?

117
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,960
Sure. Yeah. Just keep an eye on the chick and duck.

118
00:06:32,210 --> 00:06:34,130
Chick and the duck'? Didn't they die...?

119
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:40,550
Dive. Yeah, they dove. Headfirst into fun on the farm.

120
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,930
So...

121
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:54,980
Morning.

122
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:54,980
You too.

123
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:58,990
Last night was just wonderful.

124
00:06:55,150 --> 00:06:58,990
Oh, it really was.

125
00:06:59,150 --> 00:07:01,320
I woke up today with the biggest smile on my face.

126
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:03,570
I know, me too. It was...

127
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:07,490
You know, it was like one of those things you think is never gonna happen.

128
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:11,410
And then it does, and it's everything you want it to be.

129
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:14,170
I know. It was just...

130
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:18,800
It's just the perfect way to say goodbye.

131
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:30,140
Just a little bit more, honey.

132
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:30,140
Oh, man, this hurts!

133
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:32,140
Is it really that bad?

134
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:32,140
Uh-huh.

135
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:36,270
I think it's time to kick you in the nuts and see which is worse.

136
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,780
The baby's head is crowning.

137
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:45,530
Oh, my God! That is the most beautiful top of a head I have ever seen.

138
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:50,080
Chandler, you have to see this.

139
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:50,080
I'm okay.

140
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:53,210
You don't want to miss this. This is the birth of your child.

141
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:56,920
It's the miracle of life.

142
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:56,920
All right.

143
00:07:58,670 --> 00:08:02,300
Wow, that is one disgusting miracle.

144
