Hey, handsome.

157
00:08:47,050 --> 00:08:52,260
I'll love you so much that no woman is ever gonna be good enough for you.

158
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:57,060
We are so lucky.

159
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:57,060
I know.

160
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:00,400
He has your eyes.

161
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:05,440
I mean, I know that's not possible, but he does.

162
00:09:05,610 --> 00:09:08,530
We'll just get him cleaned up a bit.

163
00:09:05,610 --> 00:09:08,530
Okay.

164
00:09:10,370 --> 00:09:12,790
Oh, my God, he's beautiful.

165
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:17,040
Thank you so much.

166
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:17,040
I'm really happy for you guys.

167
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,630
How do you feel?

168
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,630
I'm tired.

169
00:09:20,790 --> 00:09:25,590
You don't have that much time to relax. The other one will be along in a minute.

170
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:34,020
I'm sorry, who should be along in a what, now?

171
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:38,310
The next baby should be along in a minute.

172
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:41,230
We only ordered one.

173
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:45,280
You know it's twins, right?

174
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:45,280
Oh, yeah.

175
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:48,900
These are the faces of two people in the know.

176
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:58,460
I can't believe you didn't know its twins. This has never happened before.

177
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:02,420
Well, gosh. That makes me feel so special and good.

178
00:10:02,590 --> 00:10:04,090
Did you know it was twins?

179
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:06,800
Yeah, it's here in the paperwork we got from the clinic.

180
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:10,090
Did anybody tell you?

181
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:10,090
I don't think so.

182
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:13,300
Although, they did mention something about two heartbeats...

183
00:10:13,470 --> 00:10:15,510
...but I thought that was just mine and the baby's.

184
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,350
They said, "Both heartbeats are strong."

185
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,940
And I thought, "Well, that's good, because I'm having a baby."

186
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:25,320
This is unbelievable.

187
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:25,320
Twins actually run in my family.

188
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,230
Interesting.

189
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:30,650
Can I see you for a second?

190
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:35,330
What do we do?

191
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:35,330
What do you mean, "What do we do?"

192
00:10:35,490 --> 00:10:39,160
Twins!

193
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:43,630
Chandler, you're panicking.

194
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:43,630
Uh-huh! Join me, won't you?

195
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:48,960
What do you say we keep one and then just have an option on the other one?

196
00:10:49,130 --> 00:10:51,760
We can't split them up.

197
00:10:49,130 --> 00:10:51,760
Why not?

198
00:10:51,930 --> 00:10:54,100
We could give each of them half a medallion.

199
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:56,890
And then years later, they'll find each other...

200
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:03,900
...and be reunited. I mean, that's a great day for everybody.

201
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:07,150
Okay. What if the person who adopts the other one is horrible?

202
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:10,320
What if they're not? What if it's adopted by a king?

203
00:11:10,530 --> 00:11:13,860
Yeah. Because I hear the king is looking to adopt.

204
00:11:14,030 --> 00:11:17,080
Monica, we are not ready to have two babies.

205
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,660
That doesn't matter. We have waited so long for this.

206
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:24,040
I don't care if it's two babies. I don't care if it's three babies.

207
00:11:24,210 --> 00:11:27,920
I don't care if the entire cast of Eight Is Enough comes out of there.

208
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,970
We are taking them home because they are our children.

209
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:36,260
Okay. Shh.

210
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:38,350
Qkay

211
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:38,350
Qkay!

212
00:11:38,510 --> 00:11:40,390
Okay.

213
00:11:40,930 --> 00:11:43,690
It looks like we're about ready over here. Come on, Erica.

214
00:11:43,850 --> 00:11:45,940
Start pushing again now.

215
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:51,030
Here she comes.

216
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:51,030
She? It's a girl?

217
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,820
Yeah.

218
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,240
Well, now we have one of each.

219
00:11:57,740 --> 00:12:00,490
And that's enough.

220
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:06,670
And then she said it was the perfect way to say goodbye.

221
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,750
Oh, my God.

222
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:10,380
What did you say?

223
00:12:10,550 --> 00:12:15,090
Nothing. What do you say to that?

224
00:12:10,550 --> 00:12:15,090
Ross, you've got to tell her how you feel.

225
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,720
No way.

226
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,720
Well, you can't just give up.

227
00:12:17,890 --> 00:12:20,180
Is that what a dinosaur would do?

228
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,190
What?

229
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,190
I'm just trying to speak your language.

230
00:12:25,730 --> 00:12:28,810
Ross, Rachel doesn't know that you even wanna get back together.

231
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:33,070
If she did, she might feel differently. She might not even go.

232
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,650
You really think so?

233
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,650
I'm telling you!

234
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:40,450
Oh, okay, this is the part of the musical where there'd be a good, convincing song.

235
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:43,500
Don't take no for an answer

236
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:47,500
Don't let love fly away

237
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:51,300
Hi.

238
00:12:47,750 --> 00:12:51,300
Can't a girl finish a song around here?

239
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,260
Hey.

240
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,260
Hi. So I dropped Emma off at my mom's.

241
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:56,340
Okay.

242
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:56,340
You're not taking her tonight?

243
00:12:56,550 --> 00:12:59,050
No, we decided that I'd go ahead and set up first...

244
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:01,310
...then my mom would bring Emma to Paris on Sunday.

245
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:03,810
Wow. Eight-hour flight with a baby. Good luck, Mom.

246
00:13:03,970 --> 00:13:07,850
Are you kidding? Eight hours with my mom talking about Atkins. Good luck, Emma.

247
00:13:10,650 --> 00:13:14,820
All right. You know what? You're right. I should at least tell her how I feel.

248
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:17,200
Ross. Wait, wait.

249
00:13:14,990 --> 00:13:17,200
What? What?

250
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,030
Could you get me a muffin?

251
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:25,000
Rachel?

252
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:25,000
Yeah?

253
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:31,750
I know you're leaving tonight, but I just have to tell you.

254
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:33,630
I love you.

255
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:39,760
Now, I don't know if that changes your plans at all.

256
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:44,390
But I thought you should know.

257
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,690
Gunther.

258
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:54,280
I love you too. Probably not in the same way.

259
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:59,700
But I do. And when I'm in a café having coffee...

260
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:03,370
...or I see a man with hair brighter than the sun...

261
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:06,870
...I'll think of you.

262
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:15,710
Bye, you guys.

263
00:14:13,290 --> 00:14:15,710
Bye.

264
00:14:18,970 --> 00:14:20,720
Qh, my God!

265
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:23,930
Unbelievable.

266
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,970
Hey, you know what might help?

267
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,970
