Sorry.

533
00:28:29,770 --> 00:28:33,740
Okay. Flight 421, Paris.

534
00:28:34,450 --> 00:28:36,950
I don't see it. Do you see it?

535
00:28:34,450 --> 00:28:36,950
No. Did we miss it?

536
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:40,450
No, no, it's impossible. It doesn't leave for another 20 minutes.

537
00:28:40,620 --> 00:28:43,200
Maybe we have the flight number wrong.

538
00:28:43,370 --> 00:28:45,330
God.

539
00:28:47,580 --> 00:28:49,290
Hello.

540
00:28:47,580 --> 00:28:49,290
Hey, it's me. Here's Ross.

541
00:28:49,460 --> 00:28:50,840
What?

542
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:53,260
Hey. Hey, listen...

543
00:28:53,460 --> 00:28:57,640
You wouldn't believe the cute noises the twins are making. Wait, listen.

544
00:28:57,840 --> 00:29:00,050
But Monica...

545
00:29:00,220 --> 00:29:04,600
Monica. Monica. Monica. Monica.

546
00:29:05,560 --> 00:29:07,350
I'm sorry. They were doing it before.

547
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:10,980
That's all right. Listen, listen.

548
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:10,980
Oh, wait, wait. Here they go again.

549
00:29:11,150 --> 00:29:15,110
Monica. Monica. Monica. Monica.

550
00:29:15,450 --> 00:29:17,030
Monica?

551
00:29:15,450 --> 00:29:17,030
Isn't that cute?

552
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:20,160
That is precious! Listen...

553
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:23,620
I need Rachel's flight information.

554
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:23,620
Oh, okay.

555
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:29,580
All right, it's flight 421. Leaves at 8:40.

556
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:29,580
I have that. It's not on the board.

557
00:29:29,750 --> 00:29:33,920
That's what it says here. Flight 421. Leaves at 8:40. Newark Airport.

558
00:29:34,130 --> 00:29:36,420
What?

559
00:29:34,130 --> 00:29:36,420
Newark Airport.

560
00:29:36,630 --> 00:29:41,100
Why? Where are you?

561
00:29:36,630 --> 00:29:41,100
JFK.

562
00:30:10,630 --> 00:30:14,210
Don't worry, you guys! We're gonna get you out of there!

563
00:30:15,210 --> 00:30:18,930
And we're also gonna buy you tiny bird hearing aids.

564
00:30:24,640 --> 00:30:27,980
Okay. Here goes.

565
00:30:32,690 --> 00:30:34,360
What's the matter?

566
00:30:35,070 --> 00:30:38,440
I need to say goodbye to the table first.

567
00:30:40,030 --> 00:30:41,860
I understand.

568
00:30:42,530 --> 00:30:44,200
Okay.

569
00:30:47,830 --> 00:30:50,210
Table...

570
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:55,550
...you have given us so many great times.

571
00:30:56,840 --> 00:31:03,470
And you guys, Jordan, Victor, Joel...

572
00:31:03,890 --> 00:31:07,350
All of you guys. What can I say?

573
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:13,020
You guys make us look good.

574
00:31:16,270 --> 00:31:19,360
You want to say anything?

575
00:31:16,270 --> 00:31:19,360
I don't know.

576
00:31:20,740 --> 00:31:25,240
Except that, for one last time...

577
00:31:25,700 --> 00:31:28,330
Good game. Good game. Good game.

578
00:31:32,370 --> 00:31:34,040
Good game.

579
00:31:32,370 --> 00:31:34,040
Yeah.

580
00:31:37,500 --> 00:31:39,510
Okay. Here we go.

581
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:49,600
I can't do it.

582
00:31:50,390 --> 00:31:52,020
Well, I can't do it either.

583
00:31:53,230 --> 00:31:56,230
Hey. Did you find them?

584
00:31:53,230 --> 00:31:56,230
Yeah. They're stuck inside the table.

585
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:59,110
And we have to bust it open, but neither of us can do it.

586
00:31:59,280 --> 00:32:04,490
Oh, well, sure. It's got to be so hard.

587
00:32:04,740 --> 00:32:06,740
I'll do it. Give me.

588
00:32:11,620 --> 00:32:14,420
Phoebe! No, no, no!

589
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:19,590
Wow, I've never gone this fast before.

590
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:23,090
Phoebe, forget it, okay? Newark is, like, an hour away.

591
00:32:23,260 --> 00:32:25,090
There's no way we'll make it in time.

592
00:32:25,340 --> 00:32:29,100
She's got her cell. You could call her.

593
00:32:25,340 --> 00:32:29,100
I am not doing this over the phone.

594
00:32:29,350 --> 00:32:31,100
You don't have any other choice.

595
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:40,360
Hello?

596
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:40,360
Rachel. Oh, good.

597
00:32:40,570 --> 00:32:42,650
By the way, did you just get on the plane?

598
00:32:42,820 --> 00:32:44,610
Yeah.

599
00:32:42,820 --> 00:32:44,610
We would have caught her...

600
00:32:44,780 --> 00:32:47,320
-...if we were at the right airport.

601
00:32:44,780 --> 00:32:47,320
Yay.

602
00:32:49,330 --> 00:32:50,870
Um, Rachel, hang on.

603
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:53,290
No. No. No.

604
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:55,210
Phoebe, is everything okay?

605
00:32:56,330 --> 00:32:57,460
Um...

606
00:32:57,630 --> 00:33:02,340
Actually, no. No. You have to get off the plane.

607
00:33:02,510 --> 00:33:04,470
What? Why?

608
00:33:02,510 --> 00:33:04,470
I have this feeling that...

609
00:33:04,630 --> 00:33:10,300
...something's wrong with it. Something is wrong with the left phalange.

610
00:33:12,310 --> 00:33:15,180
Oh, honey, I'm sure there's nothing wrong with the plane.

611
00:33:15,350 --> 00:33:20,650
Look, I have to go. I love you, and I will call you the minute I get to Paris.

612
00:33:21,650 --> 00:33:23,150
Um, ahem...

613
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:26,360
What was that?

614
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:26,360
Oh, that was just my crazy friend.

615
00:33:26,530 --> 00:33:30,070
She told me to get off the plane because she had a "feeling" that there...

616
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:33,910
...was something wrong with the left phalange.

617
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:38,330
Okay. Uh, that doesn't sound good.

618
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:38,330
Oh, I wouldn't worry about it.

619
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:41,290
She comes up with this stuff, and she's almost never right.

620
00:33:41,460 --> 00:33:44,130
But she is sometimes.

621
00:33:41,460 --> 00:33:44,130
Well...

622
00:33:46,220 --> 00:33:48,590
What are you doing?

623
00:33:46,220 --> 00:33:48,590
I can't take this plane now.

624
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:52,100
Excuse me, sir. Where are you going?

625
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:52,100
I have to get off this plane.

626
00:33:52,260 --> 00:33:56,430
Her friend has a feeling something's wrong with the left phalange.

627
00:34:00,860 --> 00:34:02,480
Could I get some peanuts?

628
00:34:04,190 --> 00:34:06,940
What's wrong with the plane?

629
00:34:04,190 --> 00:34:06,940
There's nothing wrong.

630
00:34:07,150 --> 00:34:10,030
The left phalange.

631
00:34:07,150 --> 00:34:10,030
There's no "phalange."

632
00:34:10,240 --> 00:34:12,950
Oh, my God. This plane doesn't even have a phalange.

633
00:34:14,540 --> 00:34:16,580
I'm not flying on it.

634
00:34:14,540 --> 00:34:16,580
Please sit down.

635
00:34:16,790 --> 00:34:21,210
What's going on'?

636
00:34:16,790 --> 00:34:21,210
We're getting off. There is no phalange!

637
00:34:24,750 --> 00:34:27,300
This is ridiculous. I...

638
00:34:29,550 --> 00:34:32,050
Yeah, okay.

639
00:34:39,940 --> 00:34:43,110
All right. My job here is done.

640
00:34:43,730 --> 00:34:46,650
That was impressive.

641
00:34:46,820 --> 00:34:50,450
Yeah. You didn't even use the tools for most of it.

642
00:34:51,450 --> 00:34:53,240
Yeah, they were just slowing me down.

643
00:34:53,620 --> 00:34:58,450
All right. I gotta get back to the babies. See you girls later.

644
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:05,210
Sorry about the table, man.

645
00:35:01,920 --> 00:35:05,210
Yeah.

646
00:35:05,800 --> 00:35:07,550
You gonna buy a new one?

647
00:35:08,590 --> 00:35:11,130
Probably not. No.

648
00:35:11,300 --> 00:35:14,430
I don't know how much I'm gonna want to play after you go.

649
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:20,850
Well, at least we got these little guys out.

650
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:20,850
Yeah.

651
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:23,520
Aw, we were worried about you.

652
00:35:25,820 --> 00:35:27,480
Hm.

653
00:35:27,980 --> 00:35:32,320
I guess I better get used to things crapping in my hand, huh?

654
00:35:40,960 --> 00:35:43,290
I'm gonna miss these little guys.

655
00:35:43,460 --> 00:35:45,290
It was nice having birds around again.

656
00:35:47,130 --> 00:35:50,880
Hey, you know what? Maybe we should keep them here with you.

657
00:35:51,300 --> 00:35:53,970
What?

658
00:35:51,300 --> 00:35:53,970
Yeah. We got a lot going on right now.

659
00:35:54,140 --> 00:35:57,310
And plus, here, they'd have their own room.

660
00:35:58,510 --> 00:36:00,850
I could get a goose!

661
00:36:02,390 --> 00:36:06,110
You know, I think you're set with the poultry.

662
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:10,530
Thanks, man. You hear that, you guys?

663
00:36:10,690 --> 00:36:14,740
You're gonna get to stay here. And it's good...

664
00:36:14,910 --> 00:36:17,330
...you know, because, uh...

665
00:36:17,990 --> 00:36:20,660
Because now you have a reason to come visit.

666
00:36:23,500 --> 00:36:26,710
I think there may be another reason.

667
00:36:34,550 --> 00:36:36,340
So, uh...

668
00:36:38,100 --> 00:36:42,890
Awkward hug or lame cool-guy handshake?

669
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,850
Yeah, well, you know, lame cool-guy handshake.

670
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:11,090
Ma'am, I assure you, the plane is fine.

671
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:11,090
And you fixed the phalange?

672
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:14,090
Yes. The phalange's fixed.

673
00:37:14,260 --> 00:37:18,430
In fact, we've put a whole lot of extra phalanges on board, just in case.

674
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:23,600
Paging Mr. Anderson. Mr. Josh Anderson.

675
00:37:23,770 --> 00:37:25,520
Where is she?

676
00:37:23,770 --> 00:37:25,520
I don't see her.

677
00:37:25,690 --> 00:37:27,900
Rachel! Rachel Green!

678
00:37:25,690 --> 00:37:27,900
There she is!

679
00:37:28,060 --> 00:37:31,440
Rachel! Rachel!

680
00:37:31,730 --> 00:37:35,150
Whoa, do you have a boarding pass?

681
00:37:31,730 --> 00:37:35,150
No. I just have to talk to someone.

682
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:37,110
I'm sorry. You need a boarding pass.

683
00:37:37,410 --> 00:37:41,910
No, no. But you don't...

684
00:37:37,410 --> 00:37:41,910
Rachel!

685
00:37:42,660 --> 00:37:46,040
What? Oh, my God. What are you guys doing here?

686
00:37:46,870 --> 00:37:48,920
Okay. You're on.

687
00:37:49,170 --> 00:37:52,420
What? What, Ross? Okay, you're scaring me. What's going on?

688
00:37:52,590 --> 00:37:55,460
Okay. Thing is...

689
00:37:52,590 --> 00:37:55,460
Yeah.

690
00:37:56,300 --> 00:37:58,510
Don't go.

691
00:37:56,300 --> 00:37:58,510
What?

692
00:37:58,680 --> 00:38:03,680
Please, please stay with me. I am so in love with you. Please don't go.

693
00:38:04,810 --> 00:38:07,020
Oh, my God.

694
00:38:04,810 --> 00:38:07,020
I know. I know.

695
00:38:07,180 --> 00:38:11,940
I shouldn't have waited till now to say it, but, um... That was stupid, okay? I'm sorry.

696
00:38:12,110 --> 00:38:14,980
But I'm telling you now. I love you.

697
00:38:16,110 --> 00:38:21,320
Do not get on this plane.

698
00:38:16,110 --> 00:38:21,320
Miss, are you boarding the plane?

699
00:38:21,780 --> 00:38:23,450
Hey, hey

700
00:38:23,910 --> 00:38:28,290
I know you love me. I know you do.

701
00:38:28,830 --> 00:38:30,500
Miss

702
00:38:28,830 --> 00:38:30,500
I...

703
00:38:30,670 --> 00:38:33,340
I... I have to get on the plane.

704
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:34,800
No, you don't.

705
00:38:33,500 --> 00:38:34,800
Yes, I do.

706
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:37,630
No, you don't.

707
00:38:34,960 --> 00:38:37,630
I do. They're waiting for me, Ross.

708
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:41,300
I can't do this right now, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

709
00:38:41,470 --> 00:38:43,390
Rachel.

710
00:38:43,550 --> 00:38:45,970
I'm so sorry.

711
00:39:00,950 --> 00:39:02,410
I really thought she'd stay.

712
00:39:02,660 --> 00:39:04,660
I know.

713
00:39:04,830 --> 00:39:06,950
I'm sorry.

714
00:39:20,010 --> 00:39:23,260
Well, that's it.

715
00:39:23,470 --> 00:39:24,890
Everything's packed.

716
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:28,100
Wow.

717
00:39:28,850 --> 00:39:31,190
This is weird.

718
00:39:28,850 --> 00:39:31,190
I know.

719
00:39:31,350 --> 00:39:32,600
Yeah.

720
00:39:33,190 --> 00:39:36,190
Uh, does this mean there's nothing to eat?

721
00:39:37,860 --> 00:39:39,860
I put three lasagnas in your freezer.

722
00:39:41,530 --> 00:39:43,860
I love you.

723
00:39:46,700 --> 00:39:49,370
Hey.

724
00:39:46,700 --> 00:39:49,370
Hey. Did you guys make it in time?

725
00:39:49,540 --> 00:39:53,710
Yeah, yeah. He talked to her, but, um, she got on the plane anyway.

726
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:57,550
Where's Ross?

727
00:39:57,710 --> 00:39:59,920
He went home. He didn't want to see anybody.

728
00:40:17,770 --> 00:40:21,780
Ross. Hi, it's me.

729
00:40:22,030 --> 00:40:26,740
I just got back on the plane, and I just feel awful.

730
00:40:27,070 --> 00:40:31,410
That is so not how I wanted things to end with us.

731
00:40:32,580 --> 00:40:35,580
It's just that I wasn't expecting to see you.

732
00:40:35,750 --> 00:40:39,250
And all of a sudden you're there and saying these things.

733
00:40:40,670 --> 00:40:43,670
Now I'm just sitting here and thinking...

734
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:47,600
...of all the stuff I should have said and I didn't.

735
00:40:47,850 --> 00:40:51,640
I mean, I didn't even get to tell you that I love you too.

736
00:40:52,560 --> 00:40:55,770
Because of course I do. I love you.

737
00:40:57,860 --> 00:40:59,770
I love you.

738
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:02,440
I love you.

739
00:41:02,940 --> 00:41:07,280
What am I doing? I love you.

740
00:41:09,450 --> 00:41:12,450
I've got to see you. I've got to get off this plane.

741
00:41:12,620 --> 00:41:14,370
Oh, my God.

742
00:41:14,580 --> 00:41:17,630
Okay, excuse me.

743
00:41:14,580 --> 00:41:17,630
Miss, please sit down.

744
00:41:17,790 --> 00:41:20,960
No, I'm sorry. I'm really sorry, but I need to get off the plane.

745
00:41:21,130 --> 00:41:24,170
I need to tell someone that I love them.

746
00:41:21,130 --> 00:41:24,170
I can't let you off.

747
00:41:24,340 --> 00:41:27,300
Let her off the plane!

748
00:41:27,970 --> 00:41:29,800
You have to take your seat.

749
00:41:29,970 --> 00:41:32,390
Oh, please, miss. You don't understand.

750
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:35,140
Try to understand!

751
00:41:35,310 --> 00:41:38,150
Come on, miss, isn't there any way that you can just let me off the...?

752
00:41:39,650 --> 00:41:41,520
No! No!

753
00:41:42,020 --> 00:41:46,740
Oh, my God. Did she get off the plane? Did she get off the plane?

754
00:41:48,160 --> 00:41:50,820
I got off the plane.

755
00:42:00,830 --> 00:42:02,670
You got off the plane.

756
00:42:15,020 --> 00:42:17,600
I do love you.

757
00:42:17,810 --> 00:42:20,350
I love you too, and I am never letting you go again.

758
00:42:20,560 --> 00:42:23,860
Okay. Because this is where I want to be. Okay? No more messing around.

759
00:42:24,070 --> 00:42:28,200
I don't want to mess this up again.

760
00:42:24,070 --> 00:42:28,200
Me neither. We're done being stupid.

761
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:31,030
Okay. It's you and me, all right? This is it.

762
00:42:31,200 --> 00:42:34,870
This is it. Unless we're on a break.

763
00:42:44,630 --> 00:42:46,340
Don't make jokes now.

764
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:10,400
Okay, please be careful with that. It was my grandmother's. Be careful.

765
00:43:10,610 --> 00:43:12,200
Thank you.

766
00:43:12,410 --> 00:43:15,780
If that falls off the truck, it wouldn't be the worst thing.

767
00:43:24,420 --> 00:43:26,050
Wow.

768
00:43:27,670 --> 00:43:29,380
I know.

769
00:43:29,590 --> 00:43:32,260
Seems smaller somehow.

770
00:43:33,720 --> 00:43:37,180
Has it always been purple?

771
00:43:39,730 --> 00:43:43,900
Look around, you guys. This was your first home.

772
00:43:45,150 --> 00:43:51,200
And it was a happy place, filled with love and laughter.

773
00:43:51,360 --> 00:43:56,160
But more important, because of rent control, it was a frigging steal.

774
00:43:59,910 --> 00:44:05,040
Hey, do you realize that, at one time or another, we all lived in this apartment?

775
00:44:05,630 --> 00:44:07,380
Oh, yeah. That's true.

776
00:44:07,590 --> 00:44:09,960
Uh, I haven't.

777
00:44:11,050 --> 00:44:14,300
What about that summer during college that you lived with Grandma...

778
00:44:14,470 --> 00:44:17,260
...and you tried to make it as a dancer?

779
00:44:21,980 --> 00:44:25,980
Do you realize we almost made it 10 years without that coming up?

780
00:44:30,400 --> 00:44:33,320
Oh, honey, I forgot. I promised Treeger that we'd leave our keys.

781
00:44:33,490 --> 00:44:35,740
Oh, okay.

782
00:45:09,770 --> 00:45:13,150
So I guess this is it.

783
00:45:09,770 --> 00:45:13,150
Yeah.

784
00:45:14,650 --> 00:45:16,110
I guess so.

785
00:45:18,240 --> 00:45:20,660
This is harder than I thought it would be.

786
00:45:20,830 --> 00:45:23,370
Oh, it's gonna be okay.

787
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:27,620
Come on.

788
00:45:34,970 --> 00:45:39,090
Do you guys have to go to the new house now, or do you have some time?

789
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:43,140
We got some time.

790
00:45:43,770 --> 00:45:47,730
Okay. Should we get some coffee?

791
00:45:43,770 --> 00:45:47,730
Sure.

792
00:45:48,810 --> 00:45:50,400
Where?

